---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// Placeholder until the talk on 18 Nov 2026; the full resources pack replaces it just before the talk.
const signup = 'https://bit.ly/4kvorVU';
const form = 'https://tally.so/r/BEdAeR?utm_source=early';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How do you manage AI agents as a product leader? | Saielle DaSilva"
  description="Saielle DaSilva at ProductTank Global, 18 November 2026: a working day running 26 agents as a product leader. Register, and get the resources pack."
>
  <section class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Speaking · ProductTank Global</p>
      <h1>How do you manage AI agents as a product leader?</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Saielle DaSilva went from AI skeptic to product leader of a small fleet
        of agents that build, test and ship alongside her every day, and she
        runs them the way she has always run teams. In this practical,
        screen-open session, she walks through a real working day inside her
        agentic coding organisation: the control plane that keeps 26 agents on
        budget and auditable, the build, red-team, synthesise chains that keep
        the work honest, and the daily habits that taught a product person to
        defend every architectural decision her agents make.
      </p>
      <p class="talk-when">
        Wednesday 18 November 2026, 1pm GMT (5am PT, 8am ET), online. Free,
        and recorded.
      </p>
      <p><a class="btn-primary" href={signup} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Register for the talk</a></p>
    </header>

    <h2>You'll leave with</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The daily habits that let a product person defend every architectural decision her agents make</li>
      <li>A concrete starting shape for your first agent workflow, and the questions to ask before you trust one with real work</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The resources pack</h2>
    <p>
      Everything from the talk in one place: Dualtrack Agents, the open source
      agentic product team Saielle runs, ready to install; the tools she uses;
      and the write-up. The full pack goes live here on the day.
    </p>
    <p>
      Leave your email and the pack comes to you. The same form takes
      feedback after the talk.
    </p>
    <p><a class="btn-primary" href={form} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Get the resources pack</a></p>
    <figure class="qr">
      <img
        src="/speaking/producttank-global-2026-qr.svg"
        width="200"
        height="200"
        alt="QR code linking to the resources pack sign-up form"
      />
      <figcaption>Or scan to open the form on your phone.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .talk-when {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .qr {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }
  .qr img {
    background: #fff;
    padding: 8px;
  }
  .qr figcaption {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
</style>
